      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Chondromalacia of the patella is frequently encountered in patients with anterior knee pain. Arthroscopic chondroplasty with perforation of subchondral bone remains a popular treatment alternative in spite of the inferior mechanical properties of the fibrocartilaginous tissue that this procedure is designed to promote. We report a case of cystic degeneration of the patella as a previously unrecognized complication following the procedure."},
